  # large, is built concurrently, so writes go on while it is built; that
  # cannot run in a transaction, so each of Lyra's tables is created in a
  # transaction of its own. (A concurrent build that failed leaves an invalid
  # index with the same name, which "if not exists" then keeps: drop it and
  # run the migration again.)
  disable_ddl_transaction!

